# PCLN workflow

## Session start

1. Read `docs/REPRODUCING.md` if benchmark or GPU work is in scope
2. Read `README.md` for current status and feature flags
3. Activate `.venv` (see `docs/SETUP.md`)
4. Run `pytest tests/ -q` before large training changes

## Session end

1. Update `docs/EXPERIMENTS.md` if benchmark results changed
2. Update `docs/REPRODUCING.md` only if the GPU checklist itself changes
3. Keep `README.md` as the human-facing overview

## Do not

- Create scattered markdown outside `docs/` and `README.md`
- Cite sprint / Phase 4 / pre-causal numbers as LM perplexity
- Skip saving vocab mappings in training checkpoints
- Run the locked full-data ablation on CPU-only hardware
- Fall back from WikiText-2 to Tiny Shakespeare
